  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I've developed a report servlet that implements a service deployment.  This servlet is deployed on the same Tomcat with Fedora.  It happens to be deployed within the Fedora context, but for the purposes of this bug it could be anywhere on the same server.  I was trying to make the service deployment's WSDL more portable by specifying the http:address with a relative URI.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "<wsdl:service name=\"StorageReport\">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<wsdl:port binding=\"this:StorageReport_http\" name=\"StorageReport_port\">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<http:address location=\"/fedora/storagereport\"/>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "</wsdl:port>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "</wsdl:service>",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This use of relative URIs seems acceptable according to the WSDL spec:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl#_Toc492291094"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl#_Toc492291094",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I guess I would have expected the relative URI to resolve against the Fedora context URI or perhaps the REST URI of the service operation itself (probably not needed).  What I found is that relative URIs cause a NPE in some utility code.  If a resolve step were added at the top of ServerUtility.isURLFedoraServer(String url) it would fix this issue.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "java.lang.NullPointerException",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "at fedora.server.utilities.ServerUtility.isURLFedoraServer(ServerUtility.java:130)",
       "type": "text"
